<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Habsburg dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Habsburg, Habsburgs, Habsburg Monarchy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Habsburg dynasty was one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s leading royal houses, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> for centuries and holding the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> almost continuously from the fifteenth century. A Spanish branch ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries. The Habsburgs were rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, and their monarchy evolved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, which collapsed in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty.jpg" alt="Habsburg dynasty" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Counts_of_Habsbourg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
